# Prompt format

Match `prompts/review/security.md`. One prompt per file. `prompts/<job>/<slug>.md` has id `<job>.<slug>`.

Frontmatter keys:

- `id`, `title`, `status` (`draft`, `active`, or `retired`), `use_when`, `inputs`, `output`, `tags`
- `includes`: list of `fragments/*.md` paths, or omit the key

Body sections, in order: `## Use`, `## Prompt`, `## Notes`. Each section has text.

`## Prompt` is the only text to send. Input placeholders use `{{name}}` and match `inputs`. Fragment markers use `{{include:fragments/<file>.md}}` and match `includes`.

```markdown
{{include:fragments/constraint-stay-in-scope.md}}

Diff:

{{diff}}
```

Fragments are a clause, not a full prompt. Frontmatter is `id` and `title` only. `id` is the filename without `.md`. No `## Use`, `## Prompt`, or `## Notes` headings.

On any add or edit:

1. Update `catalog.yaml` in the same change. Copy `id`, `path`, `title`, `status`, `use_when`, `inputs`, and `tags`. Leave fragments out of the catalog.
2. Run `python3 scripts/check_library.py` and fix every failure before stopping.

Keep retired prompts in the catalog with `status: retired`. Leave a retired id unused for a new prompt.
